{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning. I'll do your blood pressure and pulse quick before the doctor. Arm straight, please.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja. Just hurry, hey. I'm tired and I've still got a meeting.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Hold still. One twenty eight over seventy eight. Pulse seventy six. Oxygen sat ninety eight percent.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm. I hardly slept, so.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (NURSE): Those are fine. Doctor's ready now. Your husband can go in with you.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Thanks. Parking was chaos, hey. We went round the block twice.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Ag, not the parking. I just want this done.",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (DOCTOR): Right. What's the problem today?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): My stomach. The cramps, and my stool keeps flipping from hard to loose. That's why I came.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (DOCTOR): How long has that been going on?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm. About a year, but I can't date it. Since Diwali or after. Or last winter, or the one before. I really don't know.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (DOCTOR): Where are the cramps?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): Low down, right across the belly. They ease off once I pass a stool. And I'm bloated the rest of the time.",
  "[SEG0014] person_4 (DOCTOR): Every day?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Most days, ja. Constipated, then the next day it's loose. No pattern, it just flips.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She keeps a hot water bottle on her stomach on the couch after work.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Because it hurts. Can we stay on the point.",
  "[SEG0018] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any blood in the stool?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No. None at all.",
  "[SEG0020] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any weight loss?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I haven't lost weight. Jeans are just tight from the bloat.",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (DOCTOR): Vomiting?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (DOCTOR): Fevers?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever.",
  "[SEG0026] person_4 (DOCTOR): What work do you do?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Accounts, at a logistics firm in Durban. Err, it's been mad. New system, deadlines. I'm stressed the whole day.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She comes in, drops her bag, and she's done. Won't even chat.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): I'm exhausted. That's not a crime.",
  "[SEG0030] person_4 (DOCTOR): What medicines are you on?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Buscopan. Ten milligrams. One or two tablets when the cramp hits. Maybe three times a week.",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (DOCTOR): Anything else that was prescribed?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, colo fac. Uh, mebeverin, one thirty five milligrams three times a day. I stopped it in March. Did nothing.",
  "[SEG0034] person_4 (DOCTOR): And the fibre supplement from the chemist?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Never took that. The bottle's still sealed in the cupboard.",
  "[SEG0036] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any reactions to drugs? Allergies?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): No, never. I've taken penicillin, amoxacillin, the whole lot, and I was fine. No reaction ever.",
  "[SEG0038] person_4 (DOCTOR): Bowel cancer or coeliac in the family?",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): My uncle had bowel cancer. My mother's brother. Ages ago. That's the only one.",
  "[SEG0040] person_4 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Never have.",
  "[SEG0042] person_4 (DOCTOR): Drink?",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (PATIENT): Wine on a Friday. One glass, sometimes two. Nothing in the week.",
  "[SEG0044] person_4 (DOCTOR): Lie flat. I'll press on your abdomen.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (PATIENT): Left side's sore. Don't dig in, I'm not in the mood.",
  "[SEG0046] person_4 (DOCTOR): Abdomen's soft. Mild tenderness on the left lower side. No masses. Bowel sounds normal.",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (PATIENT): And? What is it.",
  "[SEG0048] person_4 (DOCTOR): Cramps that settle when you open your bowels, the bloating, the stool flipping. I'm calling it irritable bowel for now. Provisional. Bloods before I lock that in.",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (PATIENT): Of course. More waiting.",
  "[SEG0050] person_4 (DOCTOR): Full blood count, CRP, a coeliac screen and thyroid function. Booked for today. The nurse will draw them before you leave.",
  "[SEG0051] person_4 (DOCTOR): On the food side, smaller meals. Cut the fizzy cool drinks and the extra coffee. Keep a food diary for two weeks.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): I barely eat as it is. Fine. I'll write the diary.",
  "[SEG0053] person_4 (DOCTOR): Come back in two weeks and we'll go through the results.",
  "[SEG0054] person_1 (NURSE): Right, come with me for the bloods. Sleeve up when you're ready."
 ],
